SOCIAL MEDIA CHECK LIST

 Do's                                                                                                                                                                   |
 Verify before sharing - Check facts using reliable sources before posting news or claims  
 Use privacy settings - Set profiles to private and control who sees your posts           
 Think before posting - Consider long-term impact on future jobs/education 
 Report inappropriate content - Use platform tools to flag spam, abuse, or fake news  
 Take digital breaks - Limit screen time to maintain focus on studies    
Don'ts                                       
Don't share personal info - Avoid posting addresses, phone numbers, or exact locations 
Don't accept unknown friend requests - Be cautious of strangers or suspicious accounts 
Don't engage in cyberbullying - Never harass, troll, or spread hate online             
Don't overshare daily routines - Avoid posting real-time locations or schedules      
Don't use weak passwords - Avoid simple passwords across multiple social accounts      


Pro Tip: Follow the 60-second rule - wait 60 seconds before posting anything questionable to avoid rash decisions that could impact your professional reputation
